## 2. Deep-Dive Disproof of Candidates A & B

### Why Candidate A ("GeM Seller OrderGuard") Fails Under Scrutiny

1. **Native Portal Guardrails Already Exist:** GeM's official workflow already flags "Red Flag Buyers" (buyers with more than 30 payments delayed over 70 days) and explicitly allows sellers to reject orders from them with zero penalty. Furthermore, GeM's Incident Management (IM) dashboard already tracks Show Cause Notices (5-day response window), mutual rectification requests (where buyers give consent within 5 days to fix deviations), and automatic incident closure upon Consignee Receipt and Acceptance Certificate (CRAC) generation.
2. **Software Cannot Prevent Physical or Buyer-Side Failures:** The primary post-award failure modes on GeM are:
   - Seller cash-flow shortages (which GeM solves via GeM Sahay, providing instant OCEN loans up to ₹10 lakh / 80% PO value within 3 hours).
   - OEM stock/specification mismatches committed before bidding.
   - Government consignees delaying Provisional Receipt Certificates (PRC) or CRAC. A third-party checklist app cannot force a government consignee to sign a CRAC.
3. **The Walled-Garden Trap:** GeM uses OTP-authenticated sessions and CAPTCHAs. It does not provide self-serve OAuth APIs for third-party startups to pull seller orders. Any tool you build would require the seller to manually re-type order numbers, dates, and upload PDFs into your app and into GeM—doubling their clerical work.

### Why Candidate B (Invoice-to-Cash / Receivables Recovery) Fails Under Scrutiny

1. **Direct Indian AI Competitors Already Own the Exact Wedge:**
   - **PaisaBaki ([paisabaki.com](https://paisabaki.com/)):** Built specifically as an Indian MSME WhatsApp + Email collection workspace that works without TallyPrime. Its live product already parses Hinglish customer replies (e.g., *"50k Monday kar dunga, baki GRN ke baad"*), logs the ₹50,000 promise for Monday, tags "GRN" as the blocker, and routes only exceptions to the owner.
   - **Rallic ([rallic.ai](https://rallic.ai/)):** Runs accounting and AR collections directly inside WhatsApp, synced with Zoho Books and Razorpay. Crucially, Rallic is ₹0/month (free forever for up to 10 companies) on Rallic Books, or ₹299/month for Zoho Books sync, with a ₹100/month AI assistant. A solo student founder cannot undercut free.
   - **PraecisAI ([praecisai.in](https://praecisai.in/)):** Offers a 4-stage AI collections agent with Hindi/English AI voice calls, WhatsApp campaigns, branded PDF statements, and promise-to-pay tracking for ₹5,000/month + ₹40,000 setup.
   - **TradeSure ([tradesure.in](https://tradesure.in/)) & KindDue:** Combine vernacular AI reminder calls, WhatsApp escalation with UPI links, and B2B buyer credit checks.
   - **Zoho Books & TallyPrime 5.0+:** Both natively support automated WhatsApp payment reminders, UPI QR codes on invoices, and ageing dashboards.

